{% comment %}
  CartRules — cart page quantity guard (F5 "auto-adjust in cart").
  Add this block anywhere on the cart page template. It inlines the active
  max-quantity rules as JSON and lets cartrules-notice.js clamp quantity
  inputs client-side, matching mockup Screen 3 ("Quantity was adjusted.").
  This is best-effort scaffolding, NOT tested against a live theme/cart —
  cart markup (input selectors, line item id attributes) varies a lot
  between themes, see the TODO in assets/cartrules-notice.js.
{% endcomment %}

{% assign cache = shop.metafields.cartrules.rules_cache %}
<script type="application/json" id="cartrules-rules-data">
  {% if cache and cache.enabled != false and cache.cartNoticesEnabled != false %}{{ cache | json }}{% else %}{"rules":[]}{% endif %}
</script>
<script src="{{ 'cartrules-notice.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% comment %}
  This block is intentionally invisible on the live storefront (it only
  clamps quantity inputs client-side). But that means it renders zero
  markup, so in the theme editor merchants have no visual confirmation the
  block was added at all — surfaced by the App Store review as "widget not
  visible ... in Theme Editor". Show a small placeholder in the editor only.
{% endcomment %}
{% if request.design_mode %}
  <div class="cartrules-cart-guard cartrules-cart-guard--placeholder">
    CartRules cart quantity guard (invisible on the live storefront — enforces
    maximum-quantity rules on cart quantity inputs).
  </div>
{% endif %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cart quantity guard",
  "target": "section",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
